{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Moderate pipeline-aware increase at node0 to cover demand, small increase at node1 to prevent starvation, node2 unchanged.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and inventory+backlog<5 and pipeline<40",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and inventory+backlog<5 and pipeline<50",
          "delta": "min(3, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2",
          "delta": "0"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Stronger coordinated increase at all nodes when pipeline is low relative to recent demand, capped to avoid overshoot.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "min(6, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and pipeline<40",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and pipeline<30",
          "delta": "min(2, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Conservative increase only at node0 and node1 when backlog is positive or inventory is very low, with small deltas.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and (backlog>0 or inventory<2)",
          "delta": "min(3, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and (backlog>0 or inventory<2)",
          "delta": "min(2, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2",
          "delta": "0"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Node0 has large backlog (40) and pipeline (65) with arrival 10, so increasing orders now would only add to pipeline without immediate relief. Node1 has backlog 2 and pipeline 63, so a small increase helps clear backlog. Node2 has inventory 12 and pipeline 41, so a small decrease avoids excess inventory. This set uses pipeline-aware relaxation: boost only where backlog exists and pipeline is not excessive relative to backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>20 and pipeline>50",
          "delta": "0"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0 and pipeline<70",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory>10 and pipeline>30",
          "delta": "-2"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node0 backlog is high but pipeline is also high; a small increase (1) may help without overloading. Node1 backlog is small but pipeline is high; keep order unchanged to avoid upstream backlog. Node2 has inventory and pipeline; reduce order by 1 to prevent excess. This set is conservative and coordinated to avoid increasing downstream backlog.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>30",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0 and pipeline>60",
          "delta": "0"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory>5",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Node0 backlog is very high (40) and pipeline is 65; increasing order by 2 may help clear backlog faster, but risk of over-ordering is mitigated by pipeline awareness. Node1 has backlog 2 and pipeline 63; increase by 1 to help clear backlog. Node2 has inventory 12 and pipeline 41; decrease by 3 to reduce excess inventory and avoid upstream backlog. This set is more aggressive but still bounded.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>30 and pipeline<80",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0 and pipeline<70",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and inventory>10 and pipeline>30",
          "delta": "-3"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce orders when pipeline is high relative to recent demand, especially at upstream nodes to avoid over-ordering and excess inventory. Downstream node0 has backlog and low inventory, so allow slight increase if backlog is high.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0 and inventory < 5",
          "delta": "min(2, backlog / 7)"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and pipeline > 40",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 1 and pipeline > 40",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and pipeline > 0",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Coordinated correction: if downstream node0 has backlog, slightly increase node0 order to clear it, but reduce node1 and node2 orders to prevent upstream backlog buildup. If no backlog, reduce all orders when pipeline is high.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "min(3, backlog / 5)"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 1 and backlog == 0 and pipeline > 30",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and pipeline > 0",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog == 0 and pipeline > 30",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Growth-based adjustment: if recent demand is above baseline, increase orders modestly to avoid stockouts; if below, reduce orders to avoid excess. Also cap increases when pipeline is already high.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "growth > 1.1 and pipeline < 30",
          "delta": "min(2, (growth - 1) * 10)"
        },
        {
          "when": "growth < 0.9 and pipeline > 20",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 0 and backlog > 0",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent == 2 and pipeline > 0",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Moderate pipeline-aware relaxation: reduce orders when pipeline is high relative to recent demand, but increase if backlog is high. Node0 reduces to avoid overstocking, node1 and node2 adjust based on backlog and pipeline.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline>recent*3 and backlog<10",
          "delta": "-2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>10",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and pipeline>recent*3 and backlog==0",
          "delta": "-1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0 and pipeline>recent*3",
          "delta": "1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Aggressive backlog clearing: increase orders when backlog exists, especially downstream, but cap increases to avoid overshoot. Node0 increases if backlog high, node1 and node2 increase if backlog positive.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and backlog>5",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "pipeline>recent*4",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "explanation": "Growth-responsive coordination: scale orders with demand growth, but dampen when pipeline is excessive. Node0 increases with growth, node1 and node2 adjust based on backlog and pipeline.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and growth>1.2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "2"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and growth>1.2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==2 and growth>1.2 and backlog>0",
          "delta": "1"
        },
        {
          "when": "pipeline>recent*3.5",
          "delta": "-1"
        }
      ]
    }
  ]
}

{
  "candidates": [
    {
      "explanation": "Refinement of llm_r1_0: node0 increases order when pipeline is low relative to recent demand, capped at 4; node1 increases only when backlog is high and pipeline is low, capped at 3; node2 increases only when backlog is high and pipeline is low, capped at 2, else zero. This avoids overshooting and upstream backlog while addressing potential starvation.",
      "rules": [
        {
          "when": "agent==0 and pipeline<40 and inventory+backlog<5",
          "delta": "min(4, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
        },
        {
          "when": "agent==1 and backlog>5 and pipeline<50",
          "delta": "min(3, max(0, recent-inventory-backlog))"
